what is up everybody it's animak here  for anime opera and today i will be  breaking down the latest events  in the boku no hero story including  a major reveal about dobby's true  backstory and how he became the  psychotic villain that he is today  up until this point we've only had an  incomplete version  of dobby's backstory but now finally  we are getting the full version thanks  to rey todoroki  these new revelations will have a  massive impact on the entire todoroki  family  and the wider hero society so let's get  into it  if you enjoyed the boku no hero content  on this channel and you want us to keep  it going please leave a like  and comment it really does help and i'm  not  just saying that it really does help  with the youtube algorithm  and if you're new to anime pro or maybe  you watch our videos but you haven't  subscribed yet  make this the video that you subscribe  and hit that notification bell to turn  on  all notifications the only way to make  sure that you won't miss our videos in  the future  is to take the time to subscribe hit the  bell and then select that option that  says  all finally this video will of course  contain boku no hero manga spoilers  so please proceed with caution you have  been warned  the latest chapter starts off with a  flashback to the moment when rey and  angie first met  their marriage was always supposed to be  a quirk marriage  rey's father wanted his family to be  joined with the family of the hero who  was destined to become the future number  one  and of course angie wanted someone whose  quirk would be a perfect  pairing for his own rey agreed to this  arrangement for the sake of her family  and angie was determined to make this  happen so that his future children would  have the highest possible chance of  developing the kind of quirks that could  one day surpass  all might you really have to feel bad  for rey here because it really seems  like she was pressured to do this out of  a sense of duty to her family and not  because she actually wanted to  presumably she didn't even know endeavor  at this point so  obviously this was not a relationship  that was rooted in love  it was first and foremost a quirk  marriage  this idea of a quirk marriage is a very  interesting concept  and something that is unique to the  world of boku no hero  the obvious analogy to this in our own  world would be a political marriage  where  two families join together in order to  increase their wealth and influence  regardless of whether the two people  getting married actually want to be  together  the marriage itself is not about love it  is about  interest a quirk marriage is also about  interest  but the focus is on creating offspring  with the best  possible quirks i think this quirk  marriage concept  is a good addition to the story because  realistically  if quirks were real in our own world  this type of marriage would  definitely be a thing it just feels real  and plausible within the context of that  world  and of course this type of marriage  comes with its own unique set of  challenges  and hardships and the perfect example of  this is the todoroki family itself  back in the present time dobby appears  to be resting after basically frying his  own body  over and over again during the big fight  in jakku  even though there hasn't been a lot of  public information coming out about  endeavour  since the jakku incident dobby knows  that his father  is not dead and dobby wouldn't want  endeavor to be dead anyway he is still  obsessed with getting his revenge on  endeavor  and making endeavour suffer in the worst  ways  possible just killing his father would  be too easy  and at this point it is clear that dobby  isn't just  targeting endeavor dobby intends to take  his whole family down with him  if that's what it takes to make  endeavors suffer  this means that every single member of  the todoroki family is in danger as a  direct result of  dobby's bloodthirsty obsession and  that is when we get the rest of dobby's  backstory and the real reason why toya  became a villain  back when dabi's true identity was  finally confirmed  i speculated that the reason why  endeavour stopped training dobby and  turned his attention to shoto  wasn't because he hated dobby or because  he thought dobby wasn't strong enough  it wasn't even because endeavour didn't  think that dobby was good enough to  surpass  all might in fact endeavor fully  acknowledged that dobby was stronger  than him  and that he did in fact have the  potential to surpass  all might but the specific way in which  endeavors and race quirks combined  within toya  led to a dangerous side effect although  he inherited his father's flame quirk  and although toya's flame quirk was  actually even stronger than endeavors  toya's body did not develop a sufficient  resistance to fire  instead his body inherited his mother's  ability to tolerate  extreme cold as a result every time toya  uses his fire based quirk  he inevitably burns his own body  even after realizing this endeavors  still believed that  toya could be the one to surpass all  might  but after rey and the other children  expressed their concern  that toya's training is going to kill  him endeavour finally agreed  that toya cannot be the one to surpass  all might  the risk to toyah himself would just be  too high  so endeavour makes this decision not  because he didn't like toya or because  he didn't believe in him  but because he cared about toya in his  own strange way  and he didn't want toya to continue  hurting himself after that  angie and rey decided to have more  children and eventually shoto was born  and he happened to have the perfect  combination of his parents fire and ice  quirks  however by that point toya already had  his heart set on becoming the future  number one pro hero  and surpassing all might endeavour had  already awakened  that dream within him and toyah didn't  want to give up on his life's dream now  just because using his quirk burned his  own body a little bit  toya wanted to keep training he wanted  to keep getting  stronger and he wanted to make his  father proud  so he kept coming home with burns and  bruises which were the direct result  of his training toya clearly wasn't  getting the message  so angie decided to try a tougher  approach  angie told toya to give up on the idea  of being a hero  and to just focus on other things like  his sister fuyumi  and his brother natsuo anji said this  for toya's  own good if toya gives up on being a  hero then he won't have to deal with a  lifetime of agony as he is forced to  burn himself  over and over again just so he could use  his quirk toya was committed to becoming  a hero  and he wanted nothing more than to  surpass all might  and make his father's dream come true so  when his own father told him to give it  up toya was crushed  this made him feel inadequate and  worthless and it made him jealous  of his brother shoto shoto was the one  whom angie was now placing all of his  faith in  instead of toya and this hurt toya so  much  because he still wanted to be the one to  make his father's dream come true  eventually all of this led toya to snap  desperate to get his father's attention  and to regain his favor  toya blew up at his family and tried to  hurt  baby shoto back in the hospital in the  present time  rey says to endeavor that he is not the  one who is in the most  pain the one who is in the most pain is  toyah  and this includes both physical and  psychological pain  neglected by his parents and forced to  give up on his lifelong dream  toya eventually lost it and this set him  down on the dark path of becoming a  murderous villain  this chapter was only the first part of  dobby's true  backstory so we can assume that the rest  of the story will be told  in the next chapter i assume that  endeavour stopped young toya from  hurting shoto and the other members of  the family  but what happened after that how did  toya  end up in a fire that made everyone  think that he was dead  my guess is that after he tried to hurt  shoto  toya was forcibly kept at a distance  because  after his outburst his family was now  afraid of him  feeling neglected and betrayed by his  own family toya probably decided to  train harder than he had ever trained  before  in order to prove everyone wrong at some  point  toya probably took his training too far  and he burned himself  badly in a massive fire of his own  making  after that he was presumed dead but he  wasn't really dead  so where did he go did he fake his own  death on purpose  and disappear or did someone else find  his injured body  and rescue him and if so did this person  who rescued toya  encourage him to become a villain or was  that toya's  own decision i'm super happy that we are  finally getting dobby's true backstory  the full version and i can't wait to  find out the rest of this  tragic tale definitely let me know what  you guys think  does this more complete version of the  story change how you feel about endeavor  now that we know that he didn't directly  push toya into training too hard and  that he actually wanted to protect toya  from the side effects of his own quirk  do you think that endeavour deserves  more sympathy from the mha  fanbase or do you think that endeavour's  obsession with surpassing  all might really did push toya into  becoming a villain  at least indirectly if not directly so  endeavour still deserves the hate that  he gets  finally what will happen to dobby now  where do we go from here can dobby be  redeemed in any way  or is he doomed to live out the rest of  his life as an  unrepentant psychotic villain despite  the fact that we are now  finally getting to see the human side of  dabi through this  backstory the fact remains that the  present day dobby definitely seems  committed to going straight to hell  and taking endeavour and possibly the  rest of his family down  with him but yeah crazy stuff